# Part 3 lab — Warewulf runtime-overlay template (Chapter 2 / Chapter 4)
#
# Renders /etc/security/limits.conf on each node from its profile/node
# Tags, so RDMA-heavy "bignode" instances get the higher memlock ulimit
# their fabric drivers need for pinned registration buffers, without
# hardcoding the value per node. Import with:
#
#   wwctl overlay import limits.conf.ww bignode /etc/security/limits.conf.ww
#
# Warewulf renders this with Go's text/template syntax against the node's
# resolved Tags (profile tags merged with any per-node override).

# Managed by Warewulf — do not edit on the node itself (Chapter 2: never
# hand-edit a running node, edit the source template and rebuild/reboot).

{{ if eq .Tags.rdma_enabled "true" }}
# RDMA fabric requires pinned (locked) memory for registration buffers.
* soft memlock {{ .Tags.memlock_kb }}
* hard memlock {{ .Tags.memlock_kb }}
{{ else }}
* soft memlock 65536
* hard memlock 65536
{{ end }}

# GPU compute nodes commonly need a higher open-file limit for many
# concurrent CUDA contexts / NCCL connections.
{{ if .Tags.gpu_count }}
* soft nofile 1048576
* hard nofile 1048576
{{ end }}
